      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9efb2409_bf718792",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/ims/internal/aidl/IImsCapabilityCallback.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 1098053
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-08T17:13:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This calls back to the framework. This is currently covered by the return type in the ImsConfigImplBase#setFeatureValue and is being changed to be an async callback. The error codes are contained in ImsFeature#ImsCapabilityError. There is only one error now, we can expand this once other error types are identified.",
      "parentUuid": "7033d0e9_8f6f3cba",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "a82c0fc21355ed8a293ac0f5b6fe3d151dfd13bc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7f93f76f_7a9a8440",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/ims/internal/aidl/IImsCapabilityCallback.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1135723
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-06T23:56:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we need 2 APIs? onCapabilitiesChanged and onCapabilitiesStatusChanged ..what is the difference here?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 27,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "a82c0fc21355ed8a293ac0f5b6fe3d151dfd13bc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bea46aa2_ba3e9c28",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/ims/internal/aidl/IImsCapabilityCallback.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1098053
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-07T03:54:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "onCapabilitiesChanged will be called when the framework updates the user settings for the capabilities available for the feature, {Voice, Video, UT} to {Voice, UT}, for example. This can happen in one process (settings process) and we will need to be notified in the other processes, like telephony. Also, the process that changed the user defined capabilities should use this callback as verification for their change.\n\nonCapabilitiesStatusChanged is used by MmTtelFeature to notify the framework that the status of those capabilities (whether or not they are currently available) have changed. This is basically equivalent to the featureCapabilitiesChanged method that notifies the framework of this now.",
      "parentUuid": "7f93f76f_7a9a8440",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 27,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "a82c0fc21355ed8a293ac0f5b6fe3d151dfd13bc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "558e1761_64eb070f",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/ims/internal/aidl/IImsCapabilityCallback.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1127148
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-07T19:23:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there any use case for onCapabilitiesChanged to be invoked from an IMS Service? Can you please update the API doc with the new methods? Is IImsCapabilityCallback a refactor of FeatureConfigCallback?",
      "parentUuid": "bea46aa2_ba3e9c28",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 27,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "a82c0fc21355ed8a293ac0f5b6fe3d151dfd13bc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "710f6cbc_e2fadb83",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/ims/internal/aidl/IImsCapabilityCallback.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1098053
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-07T19:36:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, the ImsService only uses onCapabilitiesChanged internally to notify other processes when one process has changed it. \n\nI will update the doc and provide more explanation.\n\nI also am going to work on a more formal doc that will be given to IMS providers that provides more explanation and sequence diagrams as well.",
      "parentUuid": "558e1761_64eb070f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 27,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "a82c0fc21355ed8a293ac0f5b6fe3d151dfd13bc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5462eeb5_5a4c9376",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/ims/internal/aidl/IImsCapabilityCallback.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1127148
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-07T19:47:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I strongly feel clubbing the IPC part and the IMS Service\u0027s reporting of the features should not be in one module. If we want to keep them together, then I feel it would be great to refactor the methods to be able to understand the usage difference. Capabilities, features, and configs are quite confusing when used together, I believe :-)\n\nThat will be really helpful. Any ETA on the formal doc?",
      "parentUuid": "710f6cbc_e2fadb83",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 27,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "a82c0fc21355ed8a293ac0f5b6fe3d151dfd13bc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0995f75d_9fd4d070",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/ims/internal/aidl/IImsCapabilityCallback.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1098053
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-07T20:59:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No ETA yet, I wanted to finish the implementation while writing the doc. I can look at my schedule to see what is realistic.\n\nAs for feature, capability, config - I think a lot of the confusion stems from the over-use of those terms in previous revisions of the ImsService APIs. For the new APIs, I am strictly using  the following convention (please point out any place where this is not done):\n\nFeatures have capabilities and capabilities are contained in configurations. Features are top level: {MmTel, RCS}, capabilities belong to features, MmTel-\u003e{Voice, Video, Sms}, RCS-\u003e{UCE,...}. I am happy to refactor to make these APIs cleaner as well.\n\nOne more thing, IMS Features are managed in ImsRegistrationImpl, MMTel specific capabilities are managed in MmTelFeature.",
      "parentUuid": "5462eeb5_5a4c9376",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 27,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "a82c0fc21355ed8a293ac0f5b6fe3d151dfd13bc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "625fac03_4ec078aa",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/ims/internal/aidl/IImsCapabilityCallback.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1135723
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-07T21:27:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1) Currently we dont have any equivalent API for onCapabilitiesChanged, am I right?\n2) If settings process is changing any capability, it will be in this flow\nsettings-\u003efrwks (ImsManager)-\u003evendor-\u003e Modem\nModem will update back the capabilities, if anything changed, coz of step 2\n\nAre you going to have 2 copies of Capabilities now? \nOne from apps and one from modem? Do we need it that way?\nWill there be a chance they are different? If yes, then am hoping it will only be different in transitional state and eventually, they both should stay the same. \n\nPlease correct, if my udnerstanding is wrong.",
      "parentUuid": "0995f75d_9fd4d070",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 27,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "a82c0fc21355ed8a293ac0f5b6fe3d151dfd13bc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d7f5bd2_cb720967",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/ims/internal/aidl/IImsCapabilityCallback.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1098053
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-08T17:13:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1) onCapabilitiesChanged isn\u0027t handled by MmTelFeatureImpl implementation, it is handled by MmTelFeature internally to notify other processes when one process changes the values.\n2) There will be two copies of capabilities, which is the same as there is today:\n  - One that notifies the MmTelFeature of user settings, which will trigger the framework to call MmTelFeature#onSetCapabilityValues to notify the MmTelFeatureImpl of the change, and\n  - another that notifies the framework of the current MmTelFeatureImpl capability status, which will notify the framework what subset of capabilities are currently available.\n\nThey will not always be in sync, for example, the user can tell the MmTelFeature (via MmTelFeature#onSetCapabilityValues) that the capabilities are {Voice, Video, Ut}. The ImsService can then update the status of these features to {Ut}, which means that voice and video are not available at the current time. This is the equivalent of the current IImsRegistrationListener#onFeatureCapabilityChanged.",
      "parentUuid": "625fac03_4ec078aa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 27,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "a82c0fc21355ed8a293ac0f5b6fe3d151dfd13bc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
