        "id": 1047993
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-08T01:48:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What if setting some of the capabilities succeeds while others fails? Should onSetCapabilityValues() return CAPABILITY_SUCCESS? How do we interpret mCapabilities in this case, e.g. requested/accepted?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 336,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 336,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "a82c0fc21355ed8a293ac0f5b6fe3d151dfd13bc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "46f51f5f_b1853c52",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/ims/internal/feature/ImsFeature.java",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 336,
      "author": {
        "id": 1098053
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-08T17:13:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In that case, the service should return an error and ImsFeature will not store any of the changes. mCapabilities stores the user defined features, which gets updated when setCapabilities is called. The MmTelFeature can read these capabilities at any time to query the capabilities that the service should support.",
      "parentUuid": "822ae220_183efb6c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 336,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 336,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "a82c0fc21355ed8a293ac0f5b6fe3d151dfd13bc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "04aba3e2_ca61b227",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/ims/internal/feature/ImsFeature.java",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 336,
      "author": {
        "id": 1047993
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-08T18:03:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems like mCapabilities will be out of sync in that case, e.g. \n1) Initial (mCapabilities\u003dVoice)\n2) setCapabilities(Voice, Video, UT), \n3) Enabling of video succeeds while UT fails. \n4) Result: mCapabilities (Voice ), even though it should have been (Voice, Video)\n\n\nIf the semantics of the APIs is \"all\" or \"nothing\", then we will always be in sync otherwise it may get out of sync. \n\n\nIt seems that onSetCapabilityValues() is expected to synchronously set the capabilities if the call is synchronous do we still  \u0027IImsCapabilityCallback c` argument? It seems like the clients code would be simpler if the function returned error/success.",
      "parentUuid": "46f51f5f_b1853c52",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 336,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 336,
        "endChar": 42
      },
